35,2,1,talk,Rin,,"I found out that island houses are pretty cheap per night, but the all-in rates mean everyone pays the same regardless of how much they eat!","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Shunichi,,The ferry is a nightmare; it takes two whole days just to travel. The train to the spa valley is much faster at ninety minutes.,"{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Asuka,,My research shows that separate bookings last time were very uneven in price. A whole building let is much fairer as it divides evenly.,"{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Takumi,,The island houses only have one bathroom for everyone and the water gets cold! The inn baths are open almost all day.,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Toshio,,"Last year we were too separate, and the shared house year left no room for anyone to be alone. We need a middle ground.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Rin,,"@Asuka, so a whole building is better for the bill? But @Shunichi, two days of travel sounds like a long time to be on a boat!","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Asuka"",""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Shunichi,,Exactly. It's a waste of a holiday. The city or the spa town are far more practical for actually spending time at the destination.,"{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Asuka,,"@Rin, yes, a single bill is more transparent. However, all-in rates can be unfair to those who eat less.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Takumi,,"@Toshio, if the shared house was too crowded, maybe the inn is better? But I'm worried about everyone sleeping in one room on futons.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Toshio,,"@Takumi, the futon situation might be the ""crowded"" feeling I remember. A city break offers private doors, which solves the privacy issue.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Rin,,"I just want to know the final price! If we go to the city, will we have to pay for everything separately? That sounds confusing!","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Shunichi,,"@Rin, it's less confusing than spending forty-eight hours in transit. I'm leaning toward the spa town or the city for the sake of my sanity.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Asuka,,A city break with separate rooms would likely lead to the same price disparities I saw in last year's data. It's not the most logical choice.,"{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Takumi,,"I don't like the idea of a strict timetable for meals at an inn, but a single bathroom for five people on an island is even worse.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Toshio,,"If we go to the city, we risk repeating last year where people didn't even see each other from breakfast to dinner.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
